Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/pds/tif_pdsdirread.c
Line: 1086
Function: TIFFFetchExtraSamples
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: When dir->tdir_count > 10, v is allocated with _TIFFmalloc at line 1084 but the return value is not checked. If allocation fails, v is NULL and is passed to TIFFFetchByteArray (line 1086) or TIFFFetchShortArray (line 1088), which will write through v, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

